WEBVTT

01:33.190 --> 01:34.870
It's just one little brat!

01:34.870 --> 01:37.790
Surround him and stop him! 
Don't let him escape!

01:39.900 --> 01:43.090
That's right. It's just one little brat.

01:43.410 --> 01:46.660
Go on, just try to catch 
him and tear him to pieces!

01:47.520 --> 01:50.970
Gonna have to pull out all the stops!

01:50.970 --> 01:53.660
Damn it! You little...

01:53.660 --> 01:55.590
Fist Lord's Strike.

02:02.600 --> 02:03.590
Dona!

02:06.760 --> 02:09.530
I'm surprised by your 
lack of finishing blows.

02:09.910 --> 02:15.530
All you grown-ups ganging up on one little brat,
and you still can't catch him?

02:16.050 --> 02:19.000
Talk about useless!
So useless! Clearly useless!

02:19.000 --> 02:22.240
Utterly useless! Nothing but useless!

02:22.240 --> 02:29.400
I mean, we're nothing compared to 
the indiscriminate glutton Roy!

02:30.750 --> 02:36.810
Good! Nice! Wonderful! Pleasing! 
Acceptable! Agreeable!

02:36.810 --> 02:39.060
And that is precisely what makes it...

02:39.650 --> 02:42.520
gluttony!

02:42.920 --> 02:45.840
I am the spirit knight, Julius Euclius!

02:45.840 --> 02:47.020
I won't be careless!

02:48.220 --> 02:50.670
Al Clauseria!

02:52.410 --> 02:57.490
You really are exactly 
as I imagined. Splendid.

03:00.550 --> 03:01.160
What?!

03:07.060 --> 03:13.050
We idolized you, Brother, and that's a spell 
you worked your hardest to create.

03:13.050 --> 03:16.300
There's no way we wouldn't 
be familiar with it!

03:17.710 --> 03:20.220
Shut the hell up, ya moron!

03:20.220 --> 03:21.550
Wow!

03:21.550 --> 03:24.960
Here! Dog meat is best skewered!

03:24.960 --> 03:29.920
Tough, sinewy meat needs to be stabbed 
until it's tender, easy to eat,

03:29.920 --> 03:32.230
and easily transformed into manure,

03:32.230 --> 03:35.990
keeping the food chain 
going in an endless cycle!

03:35.990 --> 03:38.080
Right, Ricardo-san?!

03:38.820 --> 03:39.890
Get back!

03:39.890 --> 03:41.410
Ia! Alo!

03:43.960 --> 03:47.950
Yes, yes! We knew that fine 
feat of teamwork was coming!

03:50.080 --> 03:51.580
Nice! Nice!

03:51.910 --> 03:56.370
We are putting up a great 
fight against the two of you!

03:56.370 --> 03:59.350
This is the world we had once given up on...

03:59.670 --> 04:03.560
Oh, how unfair! How unfair! How very unfair!

04:03.560 --> 04:05.570
The hell are you blabberin' about?

04:05.570 --> 04:07.430
Creepy little brat.

04:07.840 --> 04:10.480
And how do ya know my name, anyway?!

04:11.410 --> 04:14.400
You need to keep still 
until the bleeding stops.

04:15.570 --> 04:16.860
That won't—

04:16.860 --> 04:17.360
Oh?

04:17.950 --> 04:19.450
This one is new to you, isn't it?

04:22.350 --> 04:23.530
And there it is!

04:23.960 --> 04:26.960
The genius of hard work 
and greatest of knights!

04:26.960 --> 04:32.080
You are still full of charms 
that we don't yet know about!

04:34.120 --> 04:35.420
Eclipse.

04:41.770 --> 04:43.950
We have used this strike

04:43.950 --> 04:48.050
to slay 88 other 
pretty boys like you.

04:48.050 --> 04:52.900
Did you feel it all the way down 
to the marrow in your bones, Brother?

04:55.670 --> 04:57.570
You little...

05:00.050 --> 05:02.030
Welcome home!

05:03.520 --> 05:05.000
Would you like to be a meal?

05:05.000 --> 05:06.850
A feast?

05:06.850 --> 05:08.210
Or perhaps...

05:08.210 --> 05:10.920
A grand banquet?!

05:15.010 --> 05:18.300
Sword arts, martial arts, and now magic?

05:18.300 --> 05:20.750
Just what the hell are you?!

05:20.750 --> 05:24.100
We are but a humble, nameless mage.

05:24.100 --> 05:26.910
An outcast that even our 
family takes no pride in.

05:27.760 --> 05:29.220
Or are we?!

05:38.260 --> 05:41.690
Wow! Amazing! Amazing! Amazing!

05:41.690 --> 05:44.290
It's been so long since anyone survived that!

05:44.290 --> 05:47.650
Been ages since I hurt 
like this, ya little shit!

05:48.140 --> 05:53.160
You have mastered the sword, 
martial arts, and even magic.

05:53.160 --> 05:55.170
Why did you choose evil?

05:55.170 --> 05:56.370
With your strength—

05:56.370 --> 05:58.010
I thought you'd say that!

05:58.530 --> 06:01.470
I thought you'd say that, Brother.

06:01.470 --> 06:06.270
You're the brother we know,
the brother we've put our faith in.

06:06.270 --> 06:08.760
Of course we expected you to say that.

06:08.760 --> 06:10.480
We expected it!

06:11.140 --> 06:13.930
Do you remember when we were children?

06:14.440 --> 06:17.960
When we were sick and in poor shape,

06:17.960 --> 06:22.910
and we asked you to pick an appa 
for us from the tree in the yard?!

06:24.110 --> 06:27.730
We were still so little, and so were you!

06:27.730 --> 06:30.690
You said at first that you couldn't do it!

06:31.470 --> 06:33.130
Do you remember?!

06:33.530 --> 06:35.630
You really don't remember?!

06:37.660 --> 06:41.090
What... What are you talking about?

06:42.050 --> 06:45.720
I know nothing about any of that. Nothing!

06:46.170 --> 06:50.930
We always believed it! We always felt it!

06:51.480 --> 06:55.400
That we were different... 
That we were a burden!

06:55.860 --> 06:59.110
And what has become of that now?!

06:59.110 --> 07:02.820
What a great feeling! 
So this is how it feels!

07:02.820 --> 07:05.990
Oh, it must have felt wonderful!

07:07.380 --> 07:11.450
We finally understand now!

07:12.320 --> 07:16.120
I don't understand anything about you!

07:22.130 --> 07:23.960
Come, my buds!

07:23.960 --> 07:25.450
Julius!

07:25.450 --> 07:26.960
This ends now!

07:30.630 --> 07:33.930
You picked that appa for us.

07:34.340 --> 07:38.900
And that's why we hated you so much.

07:46.980 --> 07:52.700
So how many more times will it take 
before you can actually kill me?

07:52.700 --> 07:58.400
True, even if I die a hundred deaths, 
I'm not sure I could ever kill you.

07:58.400 --> 08:01.710
But don't you think maybe you 
haven't thought this through?

08:02.920 --> 08:05.780
I knew you'd come here,

08:05.780 --> 08:09.210
which means we were prepared 
to give you a warm welcome.

08:09.210 --> 08:15.060
We had the craziest, most terrifying attack 
ready to shatter your very soul to—

08:13.590 --> 08:16.600
So go ahead and do it, then!

08:16.600 --> 08:20.190
You went to so much trouble 
preparing a warm welcome...

08:20.190 --> 08:25.030
And you guys did all that just for me, right?

08:25.030 --> 08:26.990
My principles would never allow me

08:26.990 --> 08:30.570
to turn down such thoughtfulness!

08:30.570 --> 08:33.200
Hang on! You're seriously gonna die!

08:33.200 --> 08:35.340
Dying hurts, and it's scary, y'know.

08:35.340 --> 08:37.140
Especially the first time.

08:37.140 --> 08:38.380
You don't wanna do that.

08:39.610 --> 08:43.590
You should really save your firsts 
for when the time is right.

08:43.850 --> 08:47.710
You even went out of your 
way to make a dirty joke!

08:47.970 --> 08:50.930
You really do care about me, don't you?

08:50.930 --> 08:52.810
Like hell you do!

08:52.810 --> 08:56.140
It was all a lie to trick me, wasn't it?!

08:56.140 --> 08:59.600
I won't let you get away with that!

09:03.590 --> 09:09.030
Well? Which me do you like the most?

09:14.610 --> 09:17.710
I can't love anyone.

09:21.490 --> 09:23.190
There really was a trap!

09:23.870 --> 09:27.040
We gave plenty of thought to what 
you are as we prepared it for you.

09:27.040 --> 09:30.230
Not out of love, either. Just pure animosity.

09:34.010 --> 09:37.960
Oh, my. Just for me, you say?

09:38.420 --> 09:40.280
Doesn't that...

09:41.120 --> 09:42.980
make it love?

10:05.290 --> 10:07.580
No reason ya need to hold back.

10:08.150 --> 10:10.190
I won't think a thing of it.

10:10.190 --> 10:12.240
I'm just self-conscious, you know.

10:12.240 --> 10:16.630
I don't like the idea of everyone 
talking about my face later.

10:16.630 --> 10:17.360
Oh?

10:18.570 --> 10:21.570
I never thought she'd actually 
bring the whole place down.

10:22.290 --> 10:25.230
Sure am glad you're all right.

10:25.230 --> 10:28.200
I think I secretly got crushed 
about three times, though.

10:28.630 --> 10:30.640
How's the cat-eared femboy?

10:30.640 --> 10:32.410
Thanks for your concern.

10:32.730 --> 10:33.910
I'm fine.

10:35.120 --> 10:36.520
And Lust?

10:36.520 --> 10:40.360
She's definitely buried 
under all that, but...

10:40.360 --> 10:44.490
It's a waste of time to hope 
she died under there, huh?

10:45.070 --> 10:49.470
Anastasia-sama blew her face right off 
with magic, and she was just fine.

10:50.560 --> 10:51.990
Magic?

10:51.990 --> 10:54.080
After she claimed she couldn't fight, too.

10:54.080 --> 10:55.480
Not very nice of her, huh?

10:56.470 --> 10:58.060
Wh-What are you doing?!

10:58.740 --> 11:01.680
If this is a joke, it ain't funny.

11:01.680 --> 11:03.510
What's the idea, Al-san?

11:03.750 --> 11:06.390
Don't you give me that.

11:06.390 --> 11:09.740
You did something that Anastasia 
Hoshin isn't capable of doing.

11:10.390 --> 11:12.910
What's your game here?

11:13.370 --> 11:16.100
That's enough! What's all this about?!

11:16.100 --> 11:17.790
Hey, what are you doing?

11:17.790 --> 11:21.250
Don't you realize this is no time 
for us to fight amongst ourselves?!

11:21.640 --> 11:23.210
Nothing is over yet!

11:23.210 --> 11:25.260
We can't afford to be fighting!

11:26.950 --> 11:29.510
Fine, I get it. Don't put 
yourself at risk like that.

11:29.510 --> 11:34.280
Aw, come on. You're not gonna 
start killing each other?

11:49.980 --> 11:52.320
Da-da-da-dun!

12:00.040 --> 12:03.800
Capella-chan is back!

12:03.800 --> 12:07.010
Hah! I never actually believed you were dead,

12:07.010 --> 12:09.270
but it stings a bit to see 
you took no damage at all.

12:09.270 --> 12:11.040
No, no, no!

12:11.040 --> 12:14.520
Even I was bracing myself 
for death that time.

12:14.520 --> 12:17.030
Actually, I wasn't at all!

12:17.030 --> 12:19.060
But my heart sure did skip a beat!

12:19.340 --> 12:24.330
I mean, after you hit me with 
a passionate attack like that?

12:24.330 --> 12:26.030
Of course it did!

12:26.360 --> 12:29.210
Oh, could you not jump 
to conclusions, please?

12:29.210 --> 12:34.440
I love fools like you who can't see 
or read the situation they're in!

12:34.840 --> 12:38.210
I'll take my leave for today.

12:38.210 --> 12:38.960
Huh?

12:39.240 --> 12:43.150
I said I'm not going to fight anymore.

12:43.150 --> 12:47.230
I mean, I've already done 
what I wanted to do,

12:47.230 --> 12:50.710
and I've committed your cute,
sweet faces to memory.

12:50.710 --> 12:52.410
And above all—

12:51.190 --> 12:53.160
That's what the Gospel ordered you to do?

12:54.020 --> 12:54.830
Huh?

12:57.990 --> 13:02.080
"Ordered" me? That makes it sound 
like I'm doing some book's bidding,

13:02.080 --> 13:04.060
and I don't like it.

13:04.420 --> 13:09.760
My feelings for you guys aren't directions 
from some book. They're real.

13:09.760 --> 13:11.920
Pure love!

13:13.450 --> 13:14.820
How is this pure love?!

13:15.170 --> 13:19.390
If we kill her, I bet 
Crusch-sama's body will—

13:19.390 --> 13:24.170
Confusing hope with delusion 
is something idiots do.

13:24.480 --> 13:27.630
My dragon blood and
I are two separate things.

13:27.630 --> 13:30.340
So even if I die...

13:31.540 --> 13:33.830
the blood won't go away!

13:35.050 --> 13:39.820
But if you still want to come 
after me, I can't stop you.

13:43.030 --> 13:44.270
Are you kidding me?!

13:44.710 --> 13:45.760
Demi-beasts?

13:46.150 --> 13:49.860
Huh? What'd you say? That's not a bad name!

13:50.310 --> 13:55.220
They're incomplete and ugly, alive yet dead.
That's what's so great about them!

13:56.810 --> 14:00.540
How can you do this?

14:01.020 --> 14:04.540
How can you do something so cruel?!

14:04.810 --> 14:06.220
Uh...

14:06.850 --> 14:10.760
Because no one ever told me not 
to play with corpses, I guess?

14:11.730 --> 14:13.500
No! Don't let her provoke you!

14:13.500 --> 14:14.500
Run!

14:14.500 --> 14:15.590
This way!

14:16.890 --> 14:18.140
Bastards!

14:19.100 --> 14:22.470
That's it, that's it! Go ahead and flee!

14:22.470 --> 14:24.580
If you don't keep up the fight,
more will die,

14:24.580 --> 14:27.220
and more dead bodies means more demi-beasts!

14:27.590 --> 14:31.040
So go all-out and slaughter them all!

14:36.910 --> 14:38.870
Run! Run! Run!

14:38.870 --> 14:40.120
We gotta get out of here!

14:42.720 --> 14:44.870
Someone... Someone, please...

14:45.870 --> 14:47.130
<i>Understood.</i>

14:50.150 --> 14:53.970
Ferris, I heard your voice.

14:53.970 --> 14:55.260
Reinhard!

14:56.880 --> 14:57.800
Kill them!

14:58.290 --> 15:01.260
All of them! Kill all of them!

15:01.510 --> 15:04.650
You have to give them death!

15:06.600 --> 15:10.320
Yes. I will fulfill my 
duty as the Sword Saint.

15:28.570 --> 15:31.210
Well, come on! Try and hit us!

15:31.210 --> 15:32.610
Are you all right?

15:32.610 --> 15:35.740
That brat's pretty damn good at fighting!

15:36.080 --> 15:37.700
Good at fighting?

15:37.920 --> 15:41.830
I was trained by the old gardener 
at Reinhard's place, so I can tell.

15:42.460 --> 15:45.450
His movements aren't innate talent.

15:45.450 --> 15:47.750
They're the movements of 
someone who trained for years.

15:47.750 --> 15:50.810
Trained? As young as he is?

15:51.400 --> 15:54.220
The Sin Archbishop of Gluttony...

15:54.790 --> 15:56.600
Wait, so whoever he eats...

16:01.320 --> 16:07.270
Based on that reaction, I guess 
you've figured out how we work, huh?

16:07.270 --> 16:11.910
Have I? I don't have a clue 
what you're talking about.

16:11.910 --> 16:15.050
Unspoken messages really aren't 
your strong point, you know.

16:15.050 --> 16:19.180
Maybe you should give up on being 
a merchant before you get hurt.

16:20.780 --> 16:23.050
Hicks Faltman.

16:27.630 --> 16:30.440
Dynas-san, who's that on 
the ground over there?

16:32.870 --> 16:36.150
How sad. How tragic.

16:36.150 --> 16:39.710
How heartbreaking. How dismal. 
How regrettable.

16:39.710 --> 16:41.770
And because it's so sad...

16:41.770 --> 16:44.490
Because it's just too sad...

16:44.490 --> 16:49.500
is exactly why we have to indulge 
in these one-sided reunions!

16:49.500 --> 16:51.880
Dynas-san! Who is that?!

16:51.880 --> 16:53.010
Who is it?!

16:53.010 --> 16:54.060
I don't know...

16:54.630 --> 16:56.420
I've never seen his face before!

16:56.900 --> 17:00.500
I've never... seen it... 
I'm sure I haven't...

17:00.500 --> 17:02.400
Very funny, Dynas.

17:03.510 --> 17:05.390
We're friends from way back.

17:05.710 --> 17:08.740
We were so close to getting 
our hometown all cleaned up.

17:08.740 --> 17:11.750
It hurts when you say stuff like that.

17:11.750 --> 17:13.330
Where the hell did you...

17:13.330 --> 17:16.380
We know how hard you've worked.

17:16.380 --> 17:20.240
It's not your fault you couldn't 
protect Miriam and Mary.

17:21.520 --> 17:22.530
It was just...

17:23.810 --> 17:26.060
a stroke of bad luck!

17:26.060 --> 17:27.850
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

17:28.160 --> 17:33.160
What do you know about me,
you damned monster?!

17:34.250 --> 17:37.710
He eats people's memories 
and acquires their skills.

17:37.710 --> 17:40.760
That's the Authority of Gluttony 
that consumes people's names!

17:40.760 --> 17:43.540
Good! Nice! Wonderful!

17:43.540 --> 17:45.930
Pleasing! Acceptable! Agreeable!

17:45.930 --> 17:48.770
And that is precisely what makes it...

17:48.770 --> 17:50.630
gluttony!

17:52.730 --> 17:55.720
Aren't strong emotions great?

17:55.720 --> 17:57.230
They're so rich.

17:57.680 --> 18:00.840
The sweet fragrance just oozes from them,

18:00.840 --> 18:05.110
and it feels like it makes 
your whole body tingle.

18:05.110 --> 18:07.050
You get it, don't you?

18:07.050 --> 18:09.530
Sorry, but I'm just a normal guy.

18:09.530 --> 18:13.320
I can't think of people in terms 
of how delicious they are.

18:17.450 --> 18:19.210
I need all of you to do me a favor!

18:19.210 --> 18:21.590
Please, nobody say my name!

18:23.630 --> 18:28.440
Could it be that allowing us 
to fight back all this time

18:28.440 --> 18:33.850
was your idea of preparation,
like setting the table for a meal?

18:33.850 --> 18:38.130
People with keen instincts 
are so hard to finish off.

18:38.130 --> 18:42.870
They get away with it because that makes 
them all the more tasty, but still...

18:44.010 --> 18:47.530
I realize you might think I'm putting 
myself first by asking this,

18:47.890 --> 18:49.590
but please avoid saying my name!

18:49.590 --> 18:51.240
Sorry, man,

18:51.560 --> 18:54.810
but I never knew your 
name in the first place.

18:55.370 --> 18:56.170
Huh?

18:58.720 --> 19:01.120
I apologize, internal affairs officer.

19:01.120 --> 19:03.780
I had forgotten your name, as well.

19:04.510 --> 19:07.070
Yes, yes, of course!

19:07.070 --> 19:09.970
It's not like we're actually friends,

19:09.970 --> 19:12.780
or like I'm all that important or anything!

19:12.780 --> 19:14.760
I win, damn it!

19:14.760 --> 19:16.890
Dynas and Gaston.

19:18.000 --> 19:21.110
Not bad, but not worthy of a main course.

19:21.110 --> 19:25.430
But Felt-chan got away, 
and to lose you, too...

19:25.430 --> 19:27.780
That would just be too much.

19:28.130 --> 19:31.530
Not to mention, Rui would rip us a new one.

19:31.900 --> 19:34.000
Another name I don't know...

19:34.000 --> 19:35.790
This is not easing my mind at all.

19:36.240 --> 19:37.580
Listen to me, everyone.

19:37.580 --> 19:41.340
He can eat anything he touches. If he 
touches you, consider yourself dead.

19:42.880 --> 19:45.300
Thank you for being 
considerate enough to wait.

19:45.640 --> 19:47.580
What impeccable manners you have.

19:47.580 --> 19:51.550
Every gourmand knows to wait 
until the table is set.

19:51.830 --> 19:56.790
Being discerning with food 
makes life all the richer.

19:56.790 --> 19:59.770
Now, then... time to feast!

20:10.350 --> 20:12.240
Hey, not bad!

20:12.240 --> 20:15.150
But creating an opening isn't going to—

20:20.210 --> 20:23.000
It's all about having the 
right person for the job!

20:23.000 --> 20:24.960
No matter who you are, you should know

20:24.960 --> 20:27.880
there's a proper order for 
bringing food to the table!

20:28.230 --> 20:29.970
If you ignore that...

20:29.970 --> 20:32.350
What? It ruins everything?

20:35.680 --> 20:37.790
Wow, impressive!

20:47.620 --> 20:50.630
That should have caught him off-guard, too.

20:53.440 --> 20:55.990
Oh, that's just mean.

20:56.520 --> 21:00.610
You've ruined our best clothes.

21:01.740 --> 21:05.800
If those scars are what 
made you the way you are...

21:07.840 --> 21:10.350
You gonna offer us your sympathy?!

21:10.350 --> 21:12.720
That's awfully cheap of you!

21:12.720 --> 21:15.090
If you're gonna pity us, tell us your name!

21:15.090 --> 21:19.140
Of course, there are other 
ways to get that out of you...

21:21.160 --> 21:23.600
Shall we take one at a time?

21:25.540 --> 21:27.940
Time to feast!

21:27.940 --> 21:35.580
<b>A Hideous Dinner Party</b>

21:30.240 --> 21:38.370
It's rude to start eating before everyone 
has come to the table, you know.

21:35.580 --> 21:38.350
<b>A Hideous Dinner Party</b>

21:55.300 --> 21:56.990
Is your finger all right, I suppose?

21:56.990 --> 21:59.590
Yes, though he left some tooth marks.

21:59.590 --> 22:00.100
Good.

22:01.160 --> 22:04.000
Then I need to get rid of 
this rotten brat quickly

22:04.000 --> 22:06.380
and get back to Subaru so he can carry me.

22:06.380 --> 22:09.520
Agreed. Thanks for the help, Bea—

22:10.660 --> 22:15.140
What are you doing walking around 
outside alone, Beatrice-sama?

22:16.900 --> 22:22.000
You were so stubborn about never 
leaving the forbidden library before.

22:22.000 --> 22:26.580
You only left for meals and to 
spend time with the great spirit.

22:27.320 --> 22:30.800
Well, maybe there were some exceptions, eh?

22:31.540 --> 22:35.260
Understood, I suppose. So that's the trick.

22:35.520 --> 22:40.450
Just how many people are you carrying 
inside yourself, I suppose?!

22:40.450 --> 22:41.130
Well...

22:41.780 --> 22:42.730
Don't tell me...

22:44.050 --> 22:48.190
A top employee of Margrave 
Roswaal L. Mathers,

22:48.630 --> 22:51.330
and currently an attendant 
to our one and only beloved,

22:51.330 --> 22:57.010
our dearest Natsuki Subaru, 
who will be a hero someday...

22:57.500 --> 22:58.200
Rem.

22:59.360 --> 23:01.600
Is that right?

23:01.870 --> 23:05.830
Let us see our beloved hero!

23:05.830 --> 23:11.170
Our hero was supposed to come 
and pass judgment on us!

23:11.440 --> 23:14.130
On the Sin Archbishop of Gluttony,

23:14.130 --> 23:17.970
Lye Batenkaitos!

23:19.360 --> 23:20.780
This...

23:21.820 --> 23:25.770
This is the one person we 
cannot allow to see Subaru!

23:25.770 --> 23:28.640
If Subaru sees him, he'll be hurt.

23:28.640 --> 23:30.940
The damage will be irreparable.

23:32.210 --> 23:33.150
Which is why...

23:33.800 --> 23:34.860
The two of us...

23:36.190 --> 23:38.420
have to stop him ourselves, right here!
